    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d641">

                <pb facs="0623" n="451" sameAs="frus:frus1917Supp01v01/pg451"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 763.72/5206</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in China</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Reinsch</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Peking</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1917-06-08T18:00:00+08:00">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">June 8, 1917, 6 p.m.</hi>
                        </date>
                        <lb/> [<hi rendition="#italic">Received June 8, 1.55 p.m.</hi>]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>Your telegram March 26, 4 p.m.<anchor n="1" xml:id="d641-f1"/> Though United
                    States is not formally party to the agreement excluding Chinese troops from
                    Tientsin because not at the time represented by military commander there, yet we
                    are now cooperating in the protection of Mukden Railway and, therefore, I beg to
                    request your instructions whether, in order not [?] to avoid danger of
                    conflicts, the exclusion of Chinese troops from the two unlikely [<hi
                        rendition="#italic">protective?</hi>] zones along railway, guarded by
                    foreign troops, may be enforced by us jointly with other powers.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Reinsch</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
